{
  "meta": {
    "document": "Smith County FY2026-27 Budget (posted as the “FY 2027 Proposed Budget,” version Aug 30, 2026)",
    "title": "Smith County — the money trail",
    "grand_total": 198056173,
    "year": 2026,
    "note": "Texas counties budget fund by fund. This is the county’s own “Total All Funds” for the year that began October 1, 2026 (p. 21) — every fund it appropriates, not counting a $6 million transfer to the employee health-insurance fund. The Commissioners Court adopted the budget and a tax rate of $0.374088 per $100 on September 15, 2026, by a 3–1 vote. The county’s website still posts the book titled “Proposed,” with the votes shown as “Pending” (Docket #1) — but its fund totals match news reports of the adopted budget to the dollar. The tax rate is levied on $33,211,827,069 of taxable value (p. 27). This budget raises $6,139,669 (5.77%) more property tax than last year. For context, each year’s budget cover states how much more property tax it raises than the year before: FY24 +20.01%, FY25 +12.09%, FY26 +7.22% (with the rate unchanged — rising values did it), and FY27 +5.77%."
  },
